<title>FRANCE: Schneider wins 440 mln Ffr Lebanon deal.</title>
<headline>Schneider wins 440 mln Ffr Lebanon deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>French electrical engineering company Schneider said on Monday it won a 440 million franc contract to supply the Lebanese Council for Development and Reconstruction electricity transformer sub-stations.</p>
<p>The four SF6 gas-insulated sub-stations, which  will increase electricity supply to Beirut, will be delivered within 18 to 30 months, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The project is part of the Lebanese government's plan to create a 220,000 volt network for the whole country.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 pnt</p>
</text>
